.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
.Dd October 11, 2026
.Dt DTFL_NOTIFICATOR_NOTIFY_AT 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm dtfl_notificator_notify_at ,
.Nm dtfl_notificator_next ,
.Nm dtfl_notificator_frontier
.Nd request and deliver frontier-gated notifications
.Sh LIBRARY
Timely and differential dataflow library
.Pq libdtfl , \-ldtfl
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In dtfl/timely_ops.h
.Ft void
.Fn dtfl_notificator_notify_at "dtfl_notificator *n" "dtfl_cap *cap"
.Ft bool
.Fn dtfl_notificator_next "dtfl_notificator *n" "dtfl_cap **cap" "uint64_t *count"
.Ft const uint64_t *
.Fn dtfl_notificator_frontier "const dtfl_notificator *n" "size_t input" "size_t *k"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
A
.Vt dtfl_notificator
buffers requests for notification at a capability's time and delivers
them once the operator's input frontiers pass that time.
It is handed to the logic of
.Xr dtfl_stream_unary_notify 3
and
.Xr dtfl_stream_binary_notify 3
and is valid only during that call.
.Pp
.Fn dtfl_notificator_notify_at
requests a notification at the time of
.Fa cap ,
taking ownership of
.Fa cap .
To request a notification at a future time, first obtain a delayed
capability with
.Xr dtfl_cap_delayed 3 .
.Pp
.Fn dtfl_notificator_next
delivers the next capability whose time no input frontier is still at
or before, in non-decreasing order within one delivery.
It stores the capability in
.Pf * Fa cap ,
transferring ownership to the caller, and the number of folded requests
in
.Pf * Fa count ,
and returns
.Dv true ;
it returns
.Dv false
when no notification is deliverable.
The caller releases each delivered capability with
.Xr dtfl_cap_drop 3 .
.Pp
.Fn dtfl_notificator_frontier
returns input
.Fa input Ns 's
current frontier as
.Pf * Fa k
times of the scope's class.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn dtfl_notificator_next
returns
.Dv true
and sets
.Pf * Fa cap
and
.Pf * Fa count
when a notification is deliverable, else
.Dv false .
.Fn dtfl_notificator_frontier
returns a pointer to the frontier times.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
dtfl_cap *cap; uint64_t count;
while (dtfl_notificator_next(note, &cap, &count)) {
	/* emit for cap's time */
	dtfl_cap_drop(cap);
}
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr dtfl_cap_delayed 3 ,
.Xr dtfl_stream_unary_notify 3 ,
.Xr dtfl 7
.Sh HISTORY
This is the C form of timely's
.Vt Notificator
and
.Vt FrontierNotificator .
They are public at the pinned release
.Pq Li timely-v0.31.0
and were removed upstream afterward (#819); the port keeps the pinned
behavior.
.Sh THREAD SAFETY
The notificator and its capabilities belong to the thread that runs the
worker and must not be used from another thread (PLAN section 5).
